DICTIONARY

1. Create and Print a Dictionary

PROGRAM:
student = {
    "name": "Ashif",
    "age": 18,
    "course": "B.Tech IT"
}

print(student)

2. Access Dictionary Items

PROGRAM:
student = {
    "name": "Ashif",
    "age": 18,
    "course": "B.Tech IT"
}

print(student["name"])
print(student["age"])

3. Add an Item

PROGRAM:
student = {
    "name": "Ashif",
    "age": 18
}

student["city"] = "Trichy"

print(student)

4. Change a Value

PROGRAM:
student = {
    "name": "Ashif",
    "age": 18
}

student["age"] = 19

print(student)

5. Remove an Item

PROGRAM:
student = {
    "name": "Ashif",
    "age": 18,
    "city": "Trichy"
}

student.pop("city")

print(student)

6. Get Dictionary Length

PROGRAM:
student = {
    "name": "Ashif",
    "age": 18,
    "course": "B.Tech IT"
}

print(len(student))

7. Loop Through Dictionary

PROGRAM:
student = {
    "name": "Ashif",
    "age": 18,
    "course": "B.Tech IT"
}

for key in student:
    print(key)

8. Check if Key Exists

PROGRAM:
student = {
    "name": "Ashif",
    "age": 18
}

if "name" in student:
    print("Name is available")
